### Metered Geocoding API — via the APISIX gateway (data plane)
###
### Every request below goes through the Apache APISIX proxy ({{gatewayUrl}}),
### NOT directly to the geocoder. APISIX authenticates the caller by API key,
### enforces the tenant's monthly quota, meters the call, then forwards it to the
### geocoder. The JSON responses are identical to the direct service — only the
### entrypoint and the auth/quota behaviour differ.
###
### AUTHENTICATION
###   Send your key in the  X-API-Key  header on EVERY request (all paths are
###   protected, including /health and /features).
###     401  – missing or invalid/deleted key
###     403  – key disabled, or tenant suspended
###     429  – monthly quota exceeded (hard-cap plans only; soft plans bill overage)
###
### GETTING A KEY
###   Sign in to the console (http://localhost:8088) as a tenant user and create
###   a key under "API keys" — the secret is shown once. Paste it into @apiKey.
###   (Disable/enable/delete a key there too; changes take effect within ~1s.)
###
### METERING & BILLING
###   Each served request (2xx) increments your tenant's monthly counter. Live
###   usage shows on the console within a few seconds; rejected calls (401/403/429)
###   are NOT counted. Monthly bills are generated from the recorded usage.
###
### ENDPOINTS (forwarded to the geocoder)
###   GET  /features      – which optional features are enabled
###   GET  /health        – dependency health check (keyed here)
###   GET  /autocomplete  – fast prefix suggestions
###   GET  /geocode       – full-text + vector + geo search (+ interpolation)
###   GET  /address       – structured address search (+ interpolation)
###   GET  /reverse       – reverse geocoding
###   GET  /deep/forward  – deep forward geocoding via Google Maps
###   GET  /deep/reverse  – deep reverse geocoding via Google Maps
###   GET  /describe      – AI title + description for a place
###   POST /feedback      – popularity feedback loop
###   POST /places        – add a custom place
###   POST /insert        – insert raw OSM element
###   POST /traffic/probe  – submit one GPS ping
###   POST /traffic/probes – submit a GPS trace (batch)
###   GET  /traffic/edge   – live speed for the road edge nearest a point
###
### Shared query flags: vector=true|false · ai=true|false · describe=true|false

@gatewayUrl = http://localhost:8080
#@gatewayUrl = http://84.8.102.106:8080

# Your tenant API key (create one in the console; shown once). Replace this.
@apiKey = gk_250b6017_0NLrXxtKdNdS6HJ-sq3BIpBZZr1MGCFS


# ============================================================================
# AUTH / QUOTA behaviour (try these first to see the gateway in action)
# ============================================================================

### No key → 401 Unauthorized (key-auth rejects before reaching the geocoder)
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/features

###

### Invalid key → 401 Unauthorized
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/features
X-API-Key: gk_not_a_real_key

###

### Valid key → 200 (this call is metered against your monthly quota)
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/features
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

# ============================================================================
# /features  –  Feature flags
# ============================================================================

### Report which optional features (vectors, AI) are enabled
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/features
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

# ============================================================================
# /health  –  Dependency health check (keyed when accessed via the gateway)
# ============================================================================

### ES / PostGIS / NATS / Redis / Ollama status (200 healthy, 503 degraded)
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/health
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

# ============================================================================
# /autocomplete  –  Fast prefix-based suggestions
#   q (required) · lat/lon (geo-bias) · limit (1–20, default 7)
# ============================================================================

### First few characters
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/autocomplete?q=cai
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

### Longer prefix narrows the suggestions
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/autocomplete?q=cairo
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

### Arabic prefix
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/autocomplete?q=القاه
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

### Geo-biased – prefer suggestions near downtown Cairo
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/autocomplete?q=corn&lat=30.0444&lon=31.2357
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

### Short prefix with geo-bias, raised limit (nearby restaurants)
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/autocomplete?q=rest&lat=30.0444&lon=31.2357&limit=10
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

# ============================================================================
# /geocode  –  Full-text + vector + geo-decay search
#   q (required) · lat/lon (bias) · limit (1–50) · offset · vector · ai
#   describe · effort=high|optimized
#   Response carries a `pagination` block { limit, offset, total, has_more }.
# ============================================================================

### Basic name search
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/geocode?q=makaram
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

### Geo-biased search near the Giza Pyramids
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/geocode?q=pyramids&lat=29.9792&lon=31.1342&limit=5
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

### Multi-word search with Cairo location bias
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/geocode?q=tahrir square&lat=30.0444&lon=31.2357&limit=10
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

### Text-only search, vector re-ranking disabled (faster)
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/geocode?q=alexandria&limit=10&vector=false
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

### Fuzzy / typo-tolerant search (Latin typo of an English name)
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/geocode?q=alexandira&lat=31.2001&lon=29.9187&limit=5
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

### Venue-type search near Cairo
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/geocode?q=restaurant&lat=30.0444&lon=31.2357&limit=15
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

### Address-like query: housenumber + street clauses are added automatically
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/geocode?q=10 Tahrir Street, Cairo&lat=30.0444&lon=31.2357&limit=5
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

### Arabic name search
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/geocode?q=القاهرة&limit=10
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

### Include AI descriptions (cached where available, null otherwise)
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/geocode?q=cairo tower&lat=30.0459&lon=31.2243&limit=5&describe=true
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

### Address interpolation – housenumber may be interpolated from neighbours
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/geocode?q=15 Tahrir Street, Cairo&lat=30.0444&lon=31.2357&limit=5
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

### Paginate – page 1 (check pagination.has_more), then re-request with offset += limit
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/geocode?q=makaram&limit=10&offset=0
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

### Paginate – page 2
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/geocode?q=makaram&limit=10&offset=10
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

### Effort: optimized – lean fuzzy + rescore over top hits, lighter on ES under load
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/geocode?q=tahrir square&lat=30.0444&lon=31.2357&limit=10&effort=optimized
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

# ============================================================================
# /address  –  Structured address search
#   q (required) · lat/lon · limit · postcode · city · country · describe
#   Response includes a `parsed` field showing the decomposition.
# ============================================================================

### Full address: housenumber + street + city (auto-parsed)
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/address?q=10 Tahrir Street, Cairo
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

### Street with city supplied as an explicit filter param
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/address?q=Corniche El Nil&city=Cairo&limit=10
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

### Street with country restriction
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/address?q=Nile Street&country=EG&limit=10
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

### Postcode as a hard filter combined with a street query
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/address?q=Tahrir Street&postcode=11511
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

### Arabic address – street in Arabic script
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/address?q=شارع التحرير, القاهرة
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

### Address interpolation – odd/even fallback
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/address?q=17 Corniche El Nil&city=Cairo&limit=5
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

# ============================================================================
# /reverse  –  Reverse geocoding (lat/lon → address / street / boundaries)
#   lat (required) · lon (required) · describe
# ============================================================================

### Tahrir Square, Cairo
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/reverse?lat=30.0444&lon=31.2357
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

### Near the Giza Pyramids
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/reverse?lat=29.9792&lon=31.1342
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

### Downtown Alexandria
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/reverse?lat=31.2088&lon=29.9183
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

### With AI descriptions on streets/polygons
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/reverse?lat=30.0444&lon=31.2357&describe=true
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

# ============================================================================
# /deep/forward  &  /deep/reverse  –  Deep geocoding via Google Maps
#   Resolve via Google, map to OSM tags, index, return geocode/reverse-shaped.
#   Requires GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY + ENABLE_DEEP on the geocoder (else 503).
#   forward: q, language (required) · limit · region · publish · enrich
#   reverse: lat, lon, language (required) · publish · describe
# ============================================================================

### Deep forward (English) – resolve a place via Google, index it
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/deep/forward?q=Cairo Tower&language=en&region=eg&limit=5
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

### Deep forward without publishing (just resolve + return, don't index)
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/deep/forward?q=15 Tahrir Street, Cairo&language=en&publish=false
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

### Deep reverse – resolve an address for a point via Google
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/deep/reverse?lat=30.0444&lon=31.2357&language=en
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

# ============================================================================
# /describe  –  AI-generated title + description for a place
#   osm_id (required). First call blocks until generated, then cached.
# ============================================================================

### Describe a node (blocks until ready on first call)
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/describe?osm_id=n271613766
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

# ============================================================================
# /feedback  –  Popularity feedback loop
#   osm_id (required) · boost (0.1–10.0, default 1.0)
# ============================================================================

### Default boost (+1.0)
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/feedback?osm_id=n271613766&boost=1.0
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

# ============================================================================
# /places  –  Add a custom place (published to NATS, indexed asynchronously)
# ============================================================================

### Minimal – name + coordinates
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/places
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Downtown Cafe",
  "lat": 30.0500,
  "lon": 31.2400,
  "tags": { "amenity": "cafe" }
}

###

### Restaurant with address fields
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/places
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Nile View Restaurant",
  "name_en": "Nile View Restaurant",
  "lat": 30.0444,
  "lon": 31.2357,
  "osm_type": "node",
  "admin_level": 8,
  "tags": { "amenity": "restaurant", "cuisine": "egyptian" },
  "addr_housenumber": "5",
  "addr_street": "Corniche El Nil",
  "addr_city": "Cairo",
  "addr_postcode": "11511",
  "addr_country": "EG"
}

###

# ============================================================================
# /insert  –  Raw OSM element insertion (watcher.py message format)
# ============================================================================

### Node with address tags (indexed as an address point)
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/insert
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "osm_id": "n999001",
  "osm_type": "node",
  "tags": {
    "name": "Sample Building",
    "building": "yes",
    "addr:housenumber": "42",
    "addr:street": "Tahrir Street",
    "addr:city": "Cairo",
    "addr:postcode": "11511",
    "addr:country": "EG"
  },
  "geom": { "type": "Point", "coordinates": [31.2357, 30.0444] },
  "admin_level": 0,
  "area_km2": 0.0
}

###

# ============================================================================
# LIVE TRAFFIC  –  crowdsourced GPS probes (requires ENABLE_TRAFFIC on geocoder)
#   probe ping: { lat, lon, speed?(m/s), heading?(deg), ts?(epoch seconds) }
# ============================================================================

### Submit a GPS trace (batch map-matches far better than single points)
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/traffic/probes
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "device_id": "demo-device-1",
  "points": [
    { "lat": 30.0444, "lon": 31.2357, "speed": 3.0, "ts": 1750000000 },
    { "lat": 30.0429, "lon": 31.2300, "speed": 2.5, "ts": 1750000020 },
    { "lat": 30.0410, "lon": 31.2230, "speed": 3.2, "ts": 1750000045 }
  ]
}

###

### Submit a single GPS ping (device_id is a query param)
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/traffic/probe?device_id=demo-device-3
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "lat": 30.0444, "lon": 31.2357, "speed": 4.0, "ts": 1750000000 }

###

### Inspect the current live speed for the edge nearest a point
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/traffic/edge?lat=30.0444&lon=31.2357
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

# ============================================================================
# ROUTING  –  Valhalla routing engine (proxied via APISIX gateway)
#   All routing requests are POSTs with a JSON body. Coordinates are {lat, lon}.
#   costing: auto | bicycle | pedestrian | bus | truck | motor_scooter | taxi
#   Wait for GET /status to return 200 before routing (graph build can take
#   several minutes on first start — watch: docker compose logs -f valhalla).
# ============================================================================

### Status – engine version, loaded tileset bbox, available actions
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/status
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

###

### Driving directions – Cairo (Tahrir Sq.) → Alexandria, turn-by-turn
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/route
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "locations": [
    { "lat": 30.0444, "lon": 31.2357, "type": "break" },
    { "lat": 31.2001, "lon": 29.9187, "type": "break" }
  ],
  "costing": "auto",
  "directions_options": { "units": "kilometers", "language": "en-US" }
}

###

### Driving directions in Arabic narrative – Tahrir → Giza Pyramids
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/route
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "locations": [
    { "lat": 30.0444, "lon": 31.2357 },
    { "lat": 29.9792, "lon": 31.1342 }
  ],
  "costing": "auto",
  "directions_options": { "units": "kilometers", "language": "ar-SA" }
}

###

### Multi-stop route – Tahrir → Zamalek → Heliopolis → Giza Pyramids
### "through" points don't split into legs; use "break" to force a leg split
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/route
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "locations": [
    { "lat": 30.0444, "lon": 31.2357, "type": "break" },
    { "lat": 30.0614, "lon": 31.2208, "type": "through" },
    { "lat": 30.0928, "lon": 31.3201, "type": "through" },
    { "lat": 29.9792, "lon": 31.1342, "type": "break" }
  ],
  "costing": "auto",
  "directions_options": { "units": "kilometers" }
}

###

### Optimized route (TSP) – Valhalla reorders middle waypoints to minimise drive time
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/optimized_route
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "locations": [
    { "lat": 30.0444, "lon": 31.2357 },
    { "lat": 30.0928, "lon": 31.3201 },
    { "lat": 29.9792, "lon": 31.1342 },
    { "lat": 30.0614, "lon": 31.2208 }
  ],
  "costing": "auto",
  "directions_options": { "units": "kilometers" }
}

###

### Time/distance matrix – one origin (Tahrir) to several destinations at once
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/sources_to_targets
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sources": [
    { "lat": 30.0444, "lon": 31.2357 }
  ],
  "targets": [
    { "lat": 31.2001, "lon": 29.9187 },
    { "lat": 29.9792, "lon": 31.1342 },
    { "lat": 30.0928, "lon": 31.3201 },
    { "lat": 30.0614, "lon": 31.2208 }
  ],
  "costing": "auto",
  "units": "kilometers"
}

###

### Many-to-many matrix – 3 sources × 3 targets = 9 cost cells
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/sources_to_targets
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sources": [
    { "lat": 30.0444, "lon": 31.2357 },
    { "lat": 30.0614, "lon": 31.2208 },
    { "lat": 30.0928, "lon": 31.3201 }
  ],
  "targets": [
    { "lat": 30.0479, "lon": 31.2355 },
    { "lat": 29.9792, "lon": 31.1342 },
    { "lat": 31.2001, "lon": 29.9187 }
  ],
  "costing": "auto",
  "units": "kilometers"
}

###

### Bicycle directions – Tahrir → Zamalek
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/route
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "locations": [
    { "lat": 30.0444, "lon": 31.2357 },
    { "lat": 30.0614, "lon": 31.2208 }
  ],
  "costing": "bicycle",
  "directions_options": { "units": "kilometers" }
}

